  "body": "## Finding (unaddressed PR review comment)\n\nOn PR #8025 (`fix(power-guard): detect dead systemd-inhibit child, re-engage loudly`, for issue #6534), CodeRabbit raised a **Major** stability finding that was never fixed or replied to:\n\n> **Keep the child until release is confirmed.** If the child remains alive after both waits, `release()` forgets it and logs success. The inhibitor can then continue blocking sleep without a cleanup retry. Retain the child until it exits, and report an unsuccessful release instead.\n\n- Source PR: https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8025\n- Comment: https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8025#discussion_r4511572439 (comment id 4511572439)\n- Reviewer: coderabbitai[bot], 2026-11-09T10:10:56Z\n- Location: `nixos/services/power-guard/power-guard.py`, `Inhibitor.release()` (lines 233–254 at PR head)\n\n## No-response evidence\n\n- The review thread is unresolved (GraphQL `reviewThreads` checked 2026-11-10) and has no replies — the CodeRabbit comment is the only comment in the thread.\n- PR #8025's head is unchanged since the comment: the only commit is `2a6abfda8194eb944894b5fc647778f82aa977f5` (2026-11-09T10:04:21Z, before the comment). No fix commit followed.\n- The PR is still open and the comment is more than 24 hours old, so the open-PR grace rule is expired.\n- No existing issue covers this: issue #6534 is the parent dead-child-detection issue that PR #8025 addresses; the release-path defect below is distinct. Searched open/recently-closed issues for power-guard / inhibitor / release on 2026-11-10.\n\n## Still-live evidence (PR head `2a6abfda81`, read 2026-11-10)\n\n`nixos/services/power-guard/power-guard.py`:\n\n- Line 233–234: `release()` copies `self.proc` to a local and immediately sets `self.proc = None` — the child is forgotten up front.\n- Lines 253–254: after `terminate()`, `rc = self._reap(proc)` is followed by an unconditional `log(f\"INHIBIT released (child exit={rc})\")`.\n- `_reap()` (lines 153–175) returns `proc.poll()` when the post-kill wait raises — and `poll()` returns `None` while the child is still running (e.g. stuck in uninterruptible sleep, where even SIGKILL stays pending). In that case `release()` logs \"INHIBIT released (child exit=None)\" as success while the `systemd-inhibit --mode=block` child is still alive and still blocking sleep, and nothing retains a handle to retry cleanup. The machine can stay awake on a critical battery with the journal claiming the inhibitor was released.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `release()` retains the child handle until the child's exit is confirmed (`poll()`/`_reap()` shows a real exit), and clears it / logs successful release only after that confirmation; **or** the current behavior is resolved by a documented decision recorded on this issue.\n- If the child is still alive after the existing waits, the release is reported as unsuccessful (loud log), not as \"INHIBIT released\".\n- Regression coverage: a fake child whose `poll()` still returns `None` after terminate + kill + waits exercises the retained-handle / unsuccessful-release path (the PR #8025 review also noted the inhibitor failure paths in `test_power_guard.py` lack such cases).\n",
